{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-10T22:48:38.330Z","data":{"text":"The task is complete. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Task 4: Validator failing in status, inbox, and dashboard**\n\n### Implementation (all within the task's `scope`)\n\n1. **`src/core/status/validator-failing.ts`** (new) — `readValidatorFailing(projectRoot, config)` reads `validator_ran` events of every archived change via `listChanges(projectRoot, config, ['archived'])` and task 3's `readValidatorRuns` (not edited). It leaves out `not_run` runs, orders by event timestamp, and returns `{ change, outcome, runs, error }` when the latest run failed/timed out/was unreadable, else null — so one `validated` run clears the line.\n\n2. **`src/core/status/inbox.ts`** — `NeedsYouKind` gains `validator-failing`; `NeedsYouItem` gains optional `validatorFailing: { outcome, runs, error }`. Still 246 lines, under the 250 budget.\n\n3. **`src/core/status/inbox-projection.ts`** — `readInbox` adds the needs-you item (modeled on the `after-land-failed` item) with the proposal title, sorted with the other items by id.\n\n4. **`src/core/status/inbox-text.ts`** — renders `  <id>: <title> — validator <outcome> <runs>× in a row: <error> — osq show <id>`.\n\n5. **`src/cli/status.ts`** — `statusCommand` prints `Validator <outcome> <runs>× in a row, last on <id>: <error> — osq show <id>` after the watcher, `Log:`, and after-land lines.\n\n6. **`packages/ui/src/home/labels.ts`** — `validator-failing` → `validator failing`.\n\n7. **`tests/inbox-validator-failing.test.ts`** (new) — proves all four rows of the \"Validator failing\" table, \"No validator runs\", and the label scenario through `readInbox`, `formatInboxText`, and `statusCommand` over temporary archives.\n\n### Verification\n- Task verify: **6/6 pass**\n- Proposal verify (`pnpm verify`): typechecks, build, all 157 tests, and lint **all pass**\n- No preexisting test changed; the `@scenario`/`@adr 010` tags were added to every added/changed exported function"}}
